      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9633b9bc-a893-5555-ac36-7650f768a1d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Clarence Nash, Red Coffee, Tom\n- Characters: Little Quacker, Donald Duck, Daisy Duck\n- Companies: Disney\n- Places: Watonga, Oklahoma\n- Topics: Voice acting, character voices\n\nFacts:\n- Clarence Nash was born on December 7, 1904, in the rural community of Watonga, Oklahoma.\n- Clarence Nash was an American voice actor.\n- Clarence Nash provided the distinctive voice of Disney's Donald Duck for 50 years.\n- Clarence Nash was also the voice of Daisy Duck in 1940.\n- A street in Watonga, Oklahoma, was named in honor of Clarence Nash.\n- Clarence Nash died on February 20, 1985.\n- In Little Quacker, an uncredited line by Tom was supplied by Red Coffee.\n- Red Coffee's rendition of Little Quacker's voice was mostly an impersonation of Disney's Donald Duck as performed by Clarence Nash.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a2a6760e-a2ce-5cbb-b957-a37478c957c7",
        "text": "Page: Little Quacker. Sentence: line by Tom, was supplied by (uncredited) Red Coffee; Coffee's rendition of Quacker's voice was mostly an impersonation of Disney's Donald Duck as performed by Clarence Nash.\nPage: Clarence Nash. Sentence: Clarence Charles \"Ducky\" Nash (December 7, 1904 – February 20, 1985) was an American voice actor.\nPage: Clarence Nash. Sentence: He is best known for the Disney cartoon character Donald Duck, whose distinctive voice he provided for 50 years, also known as the voice of Daisy Duck in 1940.\nPage: Clarence Nash. Sentence: He was born in the rural community of Watonga, Oklahoma, and a street in that town is named in his honor.",
